## Context
Child A of tracker 1045. Author decisions 2026-10-20 (defaults of the Fable advice): the record is a git note on the candidate merge commit (outside the tree; dyne adapts later); built in the harness as a stand-in, since git-erg 0272/0273 are not landed; the gate runs the 7 forge-required checks minus skill-lint, grep-e-guard and status-verb-guard (retirement candidates, docs/2026-10-14-ci-content-review.md) plus the skills-catalog drift check. Reuse `scripts/attribution_record.py` vocabulary for the actor; a record is a statement that can be traced, not proof.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A record on the candidate merge commit (built first, so merge-time effects such as `erg close` are inside what was checked) names time, actor, host, revision, command and its scope, and tool versions
- [ ] The gate's check set is as decided above; the choice is written in the record's scope field
- [ ] `/merge` refuses a branch with no record on its candidate commit, and a positive control shows it accepts one; the latest entry for a subject decides
- [ ] The merge is made in the background once the gate passes (forge auto-merge), so waiting costs no attention
- [ ] Nothing here requires a particular agent runtime
- [ ] Catalog regenerated and drift check clean; PR under the 15-file breaker, else split
